{"id":28600,"slug":"i-knew-her-well","title":"I Knew Her Well","year":1965,"country":"Italy","duration":115,"spine":801,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28600-i-knew-her-well","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/62e398f79d4f817613884e489db8046d/IE5uw8MoxPs6597htd7IqOPG2PjoLw_large.jpg","description":"Following the gorgeous, seemingly liberated Adriana (Divorce Italian Style’s Stefania Sandrelli) as she chases her dreams in the Rome of La dolce vita, I Knew Her Well is at once a delightful immersion in the popular music and style of Italy in the sixties and a biting critique of its sexual politics and the culture of celebrity. Over a series of intimate episodes, just about every one featuring a different man, a new hairstyle, and an outfit to match, the unsung Italian master Antonio Pietrangeli, working from a script he cowrote with Ettore Scola, composes a deft, seriocomic character study that never strays from its complicated central figure. I Knew Her Well is a thrilling rediscovery, by turns funny, tragic, and altogether jaw-dropping.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Antonio Pietrangeli","slug":"antonio-pietrangeli"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Stefania Sandrelli","role":"Adriana Astarelli","slug":"stefania-sandrelli"},{"actor":"Mario Adorf","role":"Emilio “Lunk” Ricci","slug":"mario-adorf"},{"actor":"Jean-Claude Brialy","role":"Dario Marchionni","slug":"jean-claude-brialy"},{"actor":"Joachim Fuchsberger","role":"The writer","slug":"joachim-fuchsberger"},{"actor":"Nino Manfredi","role":"Cianfanna","slug":"nino-manfredi"},{"actor":"Enrico Maria Salerno","role":"Roberto","slug":"enrico-maria-salerno"},{"actor":"Ugo Tognazzi","role":"Gigi Baggini","slug":"ugo-tognazzi"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Antonio Pietrangeli","slug":"antonio-pietrangeli"},{"role":"Story and screenplay by","person":"Antonio Pietrangeli","slug":"antonio-pietrangeli"},{"role":"Story and screenplay by","person":"Ruggero Maccari","slug":null},{"rol